# PlaceMate — General Rules

You are working on **PlaceMate**, a campus placement portal (Next.js `client/` + Express `server/`, PostgreSQL/Prisma, JWT auth).

## Read before coding

- `docs/MEMORY.md` — current project state (read FIRST)
- `docs/PRD.md` + `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — what we build and how
- `docs/DECISIONS.md` — settled decisions; never silently change an ADR
- `TASKS.md` — the task you're working on; do one task at a time
- `RULES.md` — full rulebook (this file mirrors it)

## Hard rules

- TypeScript strict; no `any` without written justification.
- Do not modify unrelated files. Do not create duplicate logic — search first.
- No new dependencies without asking.
- Present a plan before any change larger than ~50 lines.
- Definition of done: lint + typecheck + build pass; docs updated (`MEMORY.md`, `TASKS.md` checkbox).
- Report at the end: files changed, what was implemented, verification, remaining issues.

## Never

- Commit `.env` files, secrets, or keys.
- Trust client-side checks for security — the API re-checks everything.
- Change database schema without updating `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §5 and a migration.
